{"module":"Term 2","title":"Unit 9 — Environment and Ecology","description":"Pollution and protection of nature, relative pronouns, cause and effect, second conditional.","intro":"This unit is about environmental problems and what we can do to protect our planet.","objectifs":["Use environment vocabulary.","Use relative pronouns who, which, where.","Express cause and effect and use the second conditional."],"cours":[{"t":"Vocabulary","h":"<ul><li>pollution, global warming, climate change, drought, deforestation, waste, recycling, renewable energy (solar, wind)</li><li>to protect, to reduce, to reuse, to recycle, to waste</li></ul>"},{"t":"Grammar","h":"<ul><li><b>Relative pronouns</b>: <i>who</i> (people), <i>which / that</i> (things), <i>where</i> (places): <i>Noor Ouarzazate is a solar plant <b>which</b> produces clean energy.</i></li><li><b>Cause and effect</b>: because (+ clause), because of / due to (+ noun), so, as a result, therefore.</li></ul><div class=\"formula key\">Second conditional: If + past simple, … would + base verb</div><div class=\"box ex\"><span class=\"box-title\">Example</span><p>If everybody <b>recycled</b>, there <b>would be</b> less waste.</p></div>"},{"t":"Communication","h":"<ul><li>Expressing concern: “I’m worried about…”, “It’s a pity that…”</li><li>Suggesting solutions: “We should…”, “Let’s…”</li></ul>"}],"recap":"who = people, which / that = things, where = places. because + clause ; because of + noun ; so / as a result = consequence. Second conditional: If + past, would + verb (imaginary situation).","cards":[["who / which / where","people / things / places"],["because of","+ noun: because of pollution"],["Second conditional","If + past, would + verb"],["3 Rs","Reduce, reuse, recycle"]],"exercises":{"facile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"The man ___ cleans our street is very kind.","choices":["who","which","where","what"],"answer":0,"explain":"A person → who."},{"type":"direct","q":"Turning old bottles into new products is ___.","accept":["recycling"],"display":"recycling","explain":"To recycle = to process waste so it can be used again."},{"type":"qcm","q":"Energy from the sun is…","choices":["solar energy","wind energy","nuclear energy","fossil energy"],"answer":0,"explain":"Solar = from the sun."}],"moyen":[{"type":"qcm","q":"The river is polluted ___ factory waste.","choices":["because of","because","so","although"],"answer":0,"explain":"“Factory waste” is a noun → because of."},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: “This is the forest ___ we went camping.”","accept":["where"],"display":"where","explain":"A place → where."},{"type":"qcm","q":"If I ___ the president, I would ban plastic bags.","choices":["were","am","will be","would be"],"answer":0,"explain":"Second conditional: If + past (were)."}],"difficile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Find the correct sentence:","choices":["If people planted more trees, the air would be cleaner.","If people would plant more trees, the air would be cleaner.","If people plant more trees, the air would be cleaner.","If people planted more trees, the air will be cleaner."],"answer":0,"explain":"If + past simple, would + base verb."},{"type":"direct","q":"Join with a relative pronoun: “Water is precious. It is wasted every day.” → Water, ___ is wasted every day, is precious.","accept":["which"],"display":"which","explain":"A thing (non-defining clause) → which."},{"type":"qcm","q":"“There was no rain for two years. ___, the harvest was poor.”","choices":["As a result","Because","Because of","Although"],"answer":0,"explain":"“As a result” introduces a consequence."}]}}